          "statement": "<p>Let \\(S\\subseteq\\mathbb{R}\\), and let \\(f,g:S\\to\\mathbb{R}\\) be continuous on \\(S\\).</p>\n<ol type=\"a\">\n<li>Prove directly from the \\(\\varepsilon\\)–\\(\\delta\\) definition that the function \\(h:\\mathbb{R}\\to\\mathbb{R}\\), \\(h(t)=|t|\\), is continuous on \\(\\mathbb{R}\\).</li>\n<li><p>Prove that the functions \\(F,G:S\\to\\mathbb{R}\\) defined by</p>\n\\[F(x)=\\max\\{f(x),g(x)\\},\\qquad G(x)=\\min\\{f(x),g(x)\\}\\]\n<p>are continuous on \\(S\\).</p></li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Hint for (b):</strong> Express the maximum and minimum of two real numbers using addition and absolute values.</p>",
